# Line endings are part of this repo's test contract.
#
# Several suites read source files off disk and assert on multi-line excerpts
# -- CSS rule bodies, App.tsx render branches, packaged-audit fixtures. Those
# assertions match "\n"; under Git's default `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows a
# checkout hands them "\r\n" instead and they fail on line endings alone, on a
# machine where nothing is actually wrong. Without this file the suite's result
# depends on the developer's Git configuration.
#
# So the working tree is LF everywhere, on every platform, matching what Git
# already stores. Electron, Vite, and Node all read LF natively on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched by EOL conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.webp binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.wav binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.asar binary
*.zip binary
